      <section id="routine" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-4">
          The 5-Minute Posture Correction &amp; Back Pain Relief Sequence
        </h2>

        <!-- B. 40-60 WORD "ANSWER-FIRST" TL;DR SUMMARY BLOCK (52 words) -->
        <aside aria-label="Quick Answer Summary" class="bg-teal-50/80 border-l-4 border-teal-700 rounded-r-xl p-5 sm:p-6 mb-8">
          <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-800 mb-1.5">
            Clinical TL;DR Summary
          </p>
          <p class="text-slate-800 text-base leading-relaxed font-medium">
            To relieve lower back pain and correct rounded posture in 5 minutes, perform four sequential movements: 60 seconds of cat-cow spinal mobilization, 90 seconds of seated thoracic extension, 90 seconds of supine hamstring tightness release, and 60 seconds of deep core activation via dead bugs to stabilize the lumbar spine.
          </p>
        </aside>

        <!-- Step-by-Step Pure Semantic HTML List -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-2.5 py-1 bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 rounded-md">Minute 0:00 &ndash; 1:00</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-teal-700">Spinal Lubrication</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">1. Controlled Cat-Cow Mobilization</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              On hands and knees, alternate between gentle spinal flexion and extension. Synchronize breath with movement to hydrate intervertebral discs and reduce stiffness across the lumbar spine.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-2.5 py-1 bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 rounded-md">Minute 1:00 &ndash; 2:30</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-teal-700">Upper Back Extension</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">2. Chair-Back Thoracic Extension</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Sit tall with hands interlaced behind your head. Gently arch your mid-back over the top edge of your chair backrest for 5-second holds to counteract forward head posture and chest tightness.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-2.5 py-1 bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 rounded-md">Minute 2:30 &ndash; 4:00</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-teal-700">Pelvic Decompression</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">3. Supine Hamstring Tightness Release</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Lie flat and loop a towel around one foot, extending the leg upward until a mild stretch is felt. Releasing chronic hamstring tightness restores neutral pelvic tilt and unloads lower back tension.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-2.5 py-1 bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 rounded-md">Minute 4:00 &ndash; 5:00</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-teal-700">Deep Stabilization</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">4. Braced Dead-Bug Core Activation</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Press your lower back gently into the floor while slowly lowering opposite arm and leg. Deep transverse abdominis core activation builds an internal muscular corset around your spine.
            </p>
          </div>
